WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:28.660
360 billion euros in China deficit opens two days of Brussels talks short of a budget deal. This is Omni View Europe, episode 23. I'm Mira, the Nerra Network's AI host. European Union leaders are in the room for China competition, energy prices, and the budget running from 2028 to 2034. Ukraine is Friday's subject, and President Volodymyr Zelensky is invited. DW says that China gap is set to top last year's figure this year.

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:34.060
The European Commission agreed with Beijing last week to curb hybrid car imports and trade

00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:38.040
chief Morrow's Chef Chavitch's preliminary deal also covers rare earths.

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:41.080
The EU accuses China of unfair state subsidies.

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:44.400
Industry groups say the import surge is shedding factories.

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:49.700
Chancellor Friedrich Murr's and President Emmanuel Macron want tools against market distortion,

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:55.180
including a Franco-German kill switch that would cut China's access if the gap stayed unsustainable.

00:00:55.180 --> 00:01:00.960
Euro news says oil is still above $100 a barrel, even after a coordinated G7 release.

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:06.400
The international energy agency warned on Wednesday that Europe could see wholesale diesel prices

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:07.040
rise again.

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:11.980
Italian and Greek leaders want the fiscal rules loosened so governments can use temporary,

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:13.700
targeted measures on prices.

00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:18.360
More fiscally conservative states warned that would pile onto deficits in shake markets.

00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:21.460
The seven-year budget needs every member to say yes.

00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:26.060
Council President Antonio Costa wants agreement by the end of the year, so the

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:28.920
legislation can be done before January 20, 28.

00:01:29.420 --> 00:01:33.300
An Irish compromise has left the frugal camp and the governments that want a bigger

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:34.460
budget both unhappy.

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:38.840
A senior diplomat said they are not in a hurry and would rather have a good deal than a

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:39.380
fast one.

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:43.260
DW says this meeting itself is not expected to break the deadlock.

00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:47.980
A special summit is set for November, and the pressure grows before elections next year

00:01:47.980 --> 00:01:49.220
in several member states.

00:01:49.220 --> 00:01:54.420
Euro news adds that Pedro Sánchez's snap election call in Spain adds another layer

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:55.160
of uncertainty.

00:01:55.680 --> 00:02:00.260
Foreign policy chief Kaja Callas told Euro news the U.S. Russia diesel deal is a gift

00:02:00.260 --> 00:02:00.760
to Putin.

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:05.600
She said most of the money for the war comes from oil, and that Ukrainian strikes on Russian

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:08.040
refineries are defense under international law.

00:02:08.620 --> 00:02:13.280
Zelensky told Piers Morgan he feels betrayed, and that Ukraine is losing American support

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:14.800
not because of Ukrainians.

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:20.320
Euro news, citing the financial times, says U.S. negotiators asked Europe to unfree some

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:23.760
immobilize Russian state assets into a vehicle run from Washington.

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:27.300
European delegates rejected that plan in Miami last week.

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:32.400
Oversight of those assets is leverage for Europe, and a loan to Ukraine from them is due to be

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:33.660
raised in Brussels on Friday.

00:02:34.810 --> 00:02:39.350
Tens of thousands of students filled Toronto over education costs and corruption, the Guardian

00:02:39.350 --> 00:02:42.070
reports, and the March turned into fires and stones.

00:02:42.070 --> 00:02:44.930
A government building in two banks were set a light.

00:02:45.290 --> 00:02:47.470
Police answered with water cannon and tear gas.

00:02:48.010 --> 00:02:49.990
Fire took hold at the education ministry.

00:02:50.390 --> 00:02:52.170
A rifle and branch nearby burned.

00:02:52.590 --> 00:02:54.610
Bins went over, shot fronts were smashed,

00:02:54.910 --> 00:02:56.370
and dozens of people were detained.

00:02:56.970 --> 00:02:59.730
France 24 says Wednesday was a second violent night

00:02:59.730 --> 00:03:01.770
with several government buildings damaged

00:03:01.770 --> 00:03:03.070
and at least one in flames.

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:06.270
Thousands called for Prime Minister Eddie Rahma to resign

00:03:06.270 --> 00:03:08.310
and for better conditions at university.

00:03:09.441 --> 00:03:12.241
Near Marseille, the French anti-terrorism prosecutor

00:03:12.241 --> 00:03:17.081
has taken a school shooting. France 24 says an initial probe found the 14-year-old

00:03:17.081 --> 00:03:21.161
suspect appeared to belong to a group called the True Crime Community. A student

00:03:21.161 --> 00:03:25.101
opened fire with a hunting rifle that had been hidden in a guitar case. Two

00:03:25.101 --> 00:03:29.441
teachers were shot and wounded. In Serbia, Balkan Insight records a string of

00:03:29.441 --> 00:03:33.681
street attacks in the weeks before parliamentary elections on October 25th and

00:03:33.681 --> 00:03:38.341
reads them as nerves inside the ruling Serbian progressive party. In Ujice the

00:03:38.341 --> 00:03:42.061
paper says party supporters beat citizens at a protest against a visit by

00:03:42.061 --> 00:03:47.481
Alexander Vuchich, while police stood by. In Belgrade, men attacked and injured an observer

00:03:47.481 --> 00:03:53.141
from the anti-corruption agency at a ruling party stand. In Novisod, supporters led by a party

00:03:53.141 --> 00:03:58.861
candidate faced the opposition student list and tried to take a banner. Mayor Alexander Shapich was

00:03:58.861 --> 00:04:04.501
reported to have assaulted a female opposition counselor. He denied it. An N1 journalist was attacked

00:04:04.501 --> 00:04:09.741
in Belgrade, and in niche a journalist was hurt while filming a party event, with police reportedly

00:04:09.741 --> 00:04:10.981
refusing to step in.

00:04:11.541 --> 00:04:16.301
Momchilo Mariana Vitch told Balkan Insight he spent a decade doing party security that

00:04:16.301 --> 00:04:18.441
included buying votes and beating protesters.

00:04:19.574 --> 00:04:24.074
The Guardian closes a series on Poland today, with people in Warsaw talking about pay

00:04:24.074 --> 00:04:26.114
that has climbed as living costs have climbed.

00:04:26.594 --> 00:04:31.574
The Varso Tower finished four years ago and the tallest building in the European Union puts

00:04:31.574 --> 00:04:37.214
a 310-meter-spire above the Palace of Culture and Science, Joseph Stalin's gift to the city.

00:04:37.214 --> 00:04:43.254
Cesarri Bwaschic, managing director of H.B. Revis in Poland, which owns the tower, said

00:04:43.254 --> 00:04:47.254
they looked down on the palace. He treated that height as the country having got past

00:04:47.254 --> 00:04:53.034
communism into a strong economy. His colleague Natalia Kasperska said a slackline walker who

00:04:53.034 --> 00:04:57.994
crossed the 500-meter gap a few months ago made a symbolic walk from the past to the future.

00:04:58.634 --> 00:05:03.194
Leave out oil exporters and financial hubs, and the paper says Polish incomes have caught

00:05:03.194 --> 00:05:08.114
Western levels faster than anywhere else. The share of the EU average went from 40 percent

00:05:08.114 --> 00:05:14.414
in the mid-1990s to 81 percent last year. National income passed $1 trillion last year,

00:05:15.354 --> 00:05:19.834
755 billion pounds, which puts Poland among the world's 20 largest economies.

00:05:20.454 --> 00:05:25.234
International monetary fund projections show income per person soon passing Japan and Spain.

00:05:25.934 --> 00:05:30.814
Deputy Foreign Minister Margin Bozaki remembered queuing after school in the 1980s for

00:05:30.814 --> 00:05:33.814
as long as five hours for butter and meat under martial law.

00:05:34.474 --> 00:05:40.334
Solidarnosed in the Gdansk shipyards, and Pope John Paul II's pilgrimage in 1979, came

00:05:40.334 --> 00:05:45.954
before democracy in 1990, the NATO in 1999, and the EU in 2004.

00:05:47.036 --> 00:05:51.516
For years, people left to earn more abroad, and Polish plumbers became shorthand in Britain

00:05:51.516 --> 00:05:54.056
in the fights over free movement before the Brexit vote.

00:05:54.556 --> 00:05:59.396
In every year since 2021, twice as many Polish nationals have left the United Kingdom

00:05:59.396 --> 00:06:00.236
as have arrived.

00:06:00.236 --> 00:06:06.256
In 2024, Germany recorded more non-German's moving to Poland than going the other way, the

00:06:06.256 --> 00:06:07.576
first time that has shown up.

00:06:08.096 --> 00:06:12.876
Architects Yedre Kolesinski and Christof Gornitski left London, where they led the foster

00:06:12.876 --> 00:06:16.776
and partners team on the Varså, and they are now designing Warsaw's new airport.

00:06:17.296 --> 00:06:21.116
The paper calls that airport the biggest greenfield infrastructure project in Europe.

00:06:21.716 --> 00:06:26.196
Gornitski said global work can be done from Warsaw, and he wanted a family near his parents

00:06:26.196 --> 00:06:29.276
in a city he finds safer, greener, and cheaper than London.

00:06:29.276 --> 00:06:33.776
Under the tower, electric trams pass cranes and dockless e-scooters.

00:06:34.096 --> 00:06:37.596
The oldest milk bar, Prasovie, takes orders on a touchscreen.

00:06:38.176 --> 00:06:43.096
Parade Square, once asphalt for Soviet tanks, has been planted as Warsaw bids for the

00:06:43.096 --> 00:06:44.316
2040 Summer Olympics.

00:06:44.916 --> 00:06:49.496
The same piece says incoming capital has pushed living costs up and squeezed poorer people

00:06:49.496 --> 00:06:50.216
in the capital.

00:06:50.776 --> 00:06:55.116
Income inequality is among the highest in Europe, and political divisions are widening

00:06:55.116 --> 00:06:56.816
before a general election next year.

00:06:56.816 --> 00:07:03.896
Also today, Britain will put $17 million, $23 million, into repairs at Chernobyl, the

00:07:03.896 --> 00:07:06.096
Chancellor and Foreign Secretary set on Thursday.

00:07:06.676 --> 00:07:11.056
The money is for the shelter and ventilation hit by a Russian drone last year, with corrosion

00:07:11.056 --> 00:07:12.096
named as the risk.

00:07:12.616 --> 00:07:17.016
Marine Le Pen told reporters and Brussels on Wednesday that France can no longer finance

00:07:17.016 --> 00:07:17.456
Ukraine.

00:07:17.976 --> 00:07:22.356
She pointed to a high deficit in weak growth and called the country's position extremely

00:07:22.356 --> 00:07:22.996
perilous.

00:07:22.996 --> 00:07:28.336
In Waterford, John James English told RTE the attack that killed Philip and Kim English

00:07:28.336 --> 00:07:33.656
and their son's column, 12, and Jaden 8, was over a 20,000-year-old drug debt run

00:07:33.656 --> 00:07:34.576
up by someone else.

00:07:35.036 --> 00:07:38.456
A girl of 14 and a boy of six were still critically ill and Dublin.

00:07:39.096 --> 00:07:42.776
Frontex has stopped a reintegration program after spending through its budget.

00:07:43.196 --> 00:07:47.356
That pause comes as Brussels looks at a wider role for the border agency in returns.

00:07:47.356 --> 00:07:53.236
In Ireland, the Irish time says about 200 recruits pass out on Friday at the Guarda College

00:07:53.236 --> 00:07:58.676
in Templemore, and that class is set to take sworn strength past 14,800 for the first

00:07:58.676 --> 00:07:58.976
time.

00:07:59.456 --> 00:08:07.636
The count was 14,683 at the end of August, up 500 in a year, and the old record was 14,750

00:08:07.636 --> 00:08:09.216
in March 2020.

00:08:09.916 --> 00:08:14.016
Guarda Headquarters says the extra numbers have backed high visibility policing in Dublin,

00:08:14.016 --> 00:08:19.216
Cleveland, Cork, Limerick and Galway. Commissioner Justin Kelly's aim is the government target

00:08:19.216 --> 00:08:26.336
of 5,000 more guardee by 2030, about 16,500, broadly in line with police Scotland. The

00:08:26.336 --> 00:08:30.936
Garda Representative Association says that pace is nowhere near fast enough. It notes

00:08:30.936 --> 00:08:36.316
Kelly told the Public Accounts Committee the force will lean on overtime until it hits 16,500,

00:08:36.596 --> 00:08:42.176
and that 400 members have left so far this year. An earlier target was to pass 15,000 in

00:08:42.176 --> 00:08:45.456
2021 and reach 18,000 by the end of the decade.

00:08:45.996 --> 00:08:50.256
The Justice Department says Minister Jim O'Callahan is confident the highest ever number

00:08:50.256 --> 00:08:52.836
of serving Gardi will be in place by the end of this year.

00:08:53.396 --> 00:08:54.876
That's OmniView Europe for today.

